+# Fix PRD pipeline schema-divergence bug (gates.py constant + regex + tests + round-trip integration test)
+
+## Task Overview
+
+The PRD pipeline gate at `src/superclaude/cli/prd/gates.py:102-110` hard-codes a 7-name section list (`Product Capabilities`, `Technical Architecture`, `User Flows`, `Integration Points`, `Existing Documentation`, `Gap Analysis`, `Suggested Phases`) that does NOT match what the prompt at `src/superclaude/cli/prd/prompts.py:188-260` instructs the agent to emit (`EXISTING_FILES`, `PATTERNS_AND_CONVENTIONS`, `FEATURE_ANALYSIS`, `RECOMMENDED_OUTPUTS`, `SUGGESTED_PHASES`, `TEMPLATE_NOTES`, `AMBIGUITIES_FOR_USER`). The upstream skill at `src/superclaude/skills/prd/SKILL.md:267-305` documents the EXISTING_FILES schema as the source of truth. Result: every `superclaude prd run` invocation halts on step-4 gate failure. A halted TUIBBS V1 run already exists at `/config/workspace/TUIBBS-scp/docs/scp-pipeline/PRD_TUIBBS_V1.md/prd-tuibbs/`; after this fix the run resumes via `superclaude prd resume sufficiency-review` with $0 re-cost.
+
+This task applies 4 atomic edits (Edit A: rewrite the `_RESEARCH_REQUIRED_SECTIONS` constant; Edit B: widen the regex in `_check_suggested_phases_detail` from `\s+` to `[\s_]+` so the underscore-form `## SUGGESTED_PHASES` matches; Edit C: rewrite the `TestCheckResearchNotesSections` fixture in `tests/cli/prd/test_gates.py:47-86` to use the new schema; Edit E: rewrite the research-notes branch of `_make_passing_output` in `tests/cli/prd/test_e2e.py:120-148` to the new schema so the 5 e2e scenarios that feed mock subprocess output through the REAL research-notes gate continue to pass), then creates 1 new round-trip integration test at `tests/cli/prd/test_research_notes_roundtrip.py` (Edit D) that wires `build_research_notes_prompt(config)` output through `_check_research_notes_sections` and `_check_suggested_phases_detail`, closing the structural blind spot identified by finding #8 of the validator brief. Verification: `uv run pytest tests/cli/prd/ -v` + `make lint`.
+
+## Key Objectives
+
+The following objectives MUST be achieved by this task:
+
+1. **Edit A — Constant rewrite:** Replace the 7-element `_RESEARCH_REQUIRED_SECTIONS` list literal at `src/superclaude/cli/prd/gates.py:102-110` with the upstream EXISTING_FILES schema (7 names: `EXISTING_FILES`, `PATTERNS_AND_CONVENTIONS`, `FEATURE_ANALYSIS`, `RECOMMENDED_OUTPUTS`, `SUGGESTED_PHASES`, `TEMPLATE_NOTES`, `AMBIGUITIES_FOR_USER`).
+2. **Edit B — Regex widening:** Change the regex on `src/superclaude/cli/prd/gates.py:134-138` inside `_check_suggested_phases_detail` from `(?:Suggested\s+)?Phases` to `(?:Suggested[\s_]+)?Phases` so `## SUGGESTED_PHASES` (underscore form) matches.
+3. **Edit C — Test fixture rewrite:** Rewrite both methods of `class TestCheckResearchNotesSections` at `tests/cli/prd/test_gates.py:47-86` so their hand-written research-notes content uses the new EXISTING_FILES-style schema.
+4. **Edit E — E2E fake content rewrite:** Rewrite the research-notes branch of `_make_passing_output` at `tests/cli/prd/test_e2e.py:120-148` so the mock subprocess output the e2e tests feed through the real research-notes gate uses the new EXISTING_FILES-style schema in lockstep with Edit A (5 e2e scenarios consume this helper).
+5. **Edit D — New round-trip test:** Create `tests/cli/prd/test_research_notes_roundtrip.py` containing two pytest functions that assert (a) the prompt's H2-section schema equals `_RESEARCH_REQUIRED_SECTIONS`, and (b) a research-notes.md constructed from the prompt's instructed sections passes both `_check_research_notes_sections` and `_check_suggested_phases_detail`.
+6. **Verification:** `uv run pytest tests/cli/prd/test_gates.py tests/cli/prd/test_research_notes_roundtrip.py -v` (focused) passes, then `uv run pytest tests/cli/prd/ -v` (full PRD suite) passes with no regressions, then `make lint` (ruff) passes clean.
